{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787227649816081454,"compiled_state":{"alias":"carryable-basalt-beagle","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f936c500850e6627431fd5fa0ee4517ffe0ccd962bae1073945142981b628d9e","event_uuid":"7a60828b-a74b-4673-a91b-9de51a1093e7","position":{"commit_sha":"c4cc7941160a5e7e1cda40bd0a63246f242959b4","position":"1787212786661063001-7a60828b-a74b-4673-a91b-9de51a1093e7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fcfee13fb051ca2d45438aa13219aeb3850d03837dbfa23525b58306d96b4cb9","event_uuid":"79775010-5f70-4de5-827a-1785b84d72b2","position":{"commit_sha":"f62fe5cda6559d192b168a89396c430da44a270b","position":"1787214824814568001-79775010-5f70-4de5-827a-1785b84d72b2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"55a8a59c216e2c5f0dff18dc9d9bfc658d0c5fa21dae889ac3c63168500a3ce4","event_uuid":"8f36580d-e781-4667-bf95-09bf2630004c","position":{"commit_sha":"f453422ef9409a76a01b01cb498fbaa820ecbc95","position":"1787214831303065001-8f36580d-e781-4667-bf95-09bf2630004c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787212786661063001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8f36580d-e781-4667-bf95-09bf2630004c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"bbb7-812e-4fe4-465d"}],"description":"## Problem\n`tests/conftest.py`'s autouse `_no_repo_root_leaks` fixture (line 297) **deletes files it did not\ncreate**, using a before/after directory snapshot that cannot distinguish a leaking test from a\nconcurrent process making a legitimate write.\n\n```python\nbefore = _repo_leak_snapshot(_REPO_ROOT)          # :300\n...\nafter = _repo_leak_snapshot(_REPO_ROOT)           # :304\nleaked = {name for name in (after - before) if not _is_coverage_artifact(name)}\nfor name in sorted(leaked, key=len, reverse=True):\n    target = _REPO_ROOT / name\n    if target.is_dir():\n        shutil.rmtree(target, ignore_errors=True)  # :313\n    else:\n        target.unlink()                            # :316\n```\n\nAnything that appears under `_REPO_ROOT` between the two snapshots is deleted. The fixture's own\ncomment says cleanup is \"best-effort\" and suppresses `OSError` so a race cannot mask the real\nfailure — sound reasoning for the leak it was built to catch, but it means a deletion that hits an\nunintended target is **silent**.\n\n## Why this is dangerous in THIS repository specifically\nrebar's ticket store lives **under the repo root** (`.tickets-*`), and rebar writes to it constantly\n— every `comment`, `edit`, `set-file-impact`, `claim`, `transition`. This project also runs many\nagents concurrently, each in its own worktree but frequently issuing `rebar` commands while a suite\nruns. A tracker write landing under a worktree's `_REPO_ROOT` during a test is, to this fixture,\nindistinguishable from a leak — and gets deleted.\n\nThis is not theoretical. Multiple agents in the 2026-08-19/20 session reported this guard firing\nbecause of concurrent `rebar` writes, e.g. \"one leak guard tripped because a `rebar transition` wrote\n`.rebar/workflow_runs` mid-run\", and \"`.tickets-tracker` written under that same worktree root\nmid-run\". Every one of those reports was treated as harmless noise. The deletion half was noticed\nonly when one agent read the fixture and observed that it **removes** what it flags — so running\nrebar tracker writes during a suite in the same worktree is *actively unsafe, not merely noisy*.\n\n## Bounding the damage honestly\nTicket events auto-commit and auto-push to `sync.remote` on write, so an event that completed its\npush survives on the remote even if the local file is deleted. The exposure is the window between\nthe write landing on disk and its push completing — plus any local-only state the fixture removes\n(`.rebar/workflow_runs` and similar are not ticket events and have no remote copy).\n\nSo this is not \"the tracker gets destroyed\". It is: a test fixture can silently delete another\nprocess's files, in a repo whose primary datastore lives at that path, with no attribution check and\nsuppressed errors. The blast radius is bounded by the auto-push, not by the fixture's design.\n\n## The design gap\nThe fixture asks \"what appeared under REPO_ROOT during this test?\" when the question it needs is\n\"what did THIS TEST create?\". A snapshot diff cannot answer the second in the presence of any other\nwriter.\n\nCandidate remedies, to be decided on evidence rather than assumed:\n- **Attribute before deleting** — only remove paths the test's own process created, or that match\n  the known leak shapes, rather than any diff entry.\n- **Fail without deleting** — the `pytest.fail()` already surfaces the leak; deletion is a\n  convenience. Removing it converts a silent data-loss risk into a loud, harmless failure. The\n  burden of proof should be on keeping the deletion, not on removing it.\n- **Exclude the datastore** — never delete under `.tickets-*` / `.rebar/`, on the grounds that no\n  legitimate test leak lives there and every legitimate concurrent write does.\n- **Detect concurrent writers** and skip cleanup when one is active.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A concurrent, legitimate write under `_REPO_ROOT` during a test run is NOT deleted — proven by\n      a test that writes from a separate process mid-test and asserts the file survives.\n- [ ] The fixture still catches the leak it exists for: a test that genuinely leaks into REPO_ROOT\n      still FAILS. Prove it by seeding a leaking test and observing the failure, so this does not\n      become a silent weakening of the guard.\n- [ ] If deletion is retained in any form, deletions are ATTRIBUTED (the fixture can say why it\n      believes it created each removed path) and are no longer silent on error.\n- [ ] Guidance records whether running `rebar` commands against a worktree while its suite runs is\n      supported. If it is not, say so in `docs/local-dev-env.md` — several agents did it all session\n      believing the resulting errors were cosmetic.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n      reports `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`.\n\n## Provenance\nFixture behaviour read directly at `tests/conftest.py:296-320` on origin/main; the concurrent-write\nreports are from four separate agents' own logs during the 2026-08-19/20 session. Surfaced by the\nimplementer on `dirt-prior-falcon`, which flagged the deletion rather than absorbing it.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"_no_repo_root_leaks at :297 deletes any path appearing under REPO_ROOT during a test, with suppressed errors and no attribution to the test that supposedly leaked it."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"746c-185a-0e48-4b83","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Leak-guard fixture deletes files it did not create, including concurrent tracker writes under REPO_ROOT","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7a60828b-a74b-4673-a91b-9de51a1093e7","79775010-5f70-4de5-827a-1785b84d72b2","8f36580d-e781-4667-bf95-09bf2630004c"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787227649816081454,"uuid":"b9c2925a-c741-4152-a569-d3ea0f84c56e"}